{
  "info": {
    "name": "PucePark · vía nginx (puerto único 80)",
    "description": "Colección completa del backend PucePark accediendo por el reverse proxy nginx en http://localhost (puerto 80).\n\nArquitectura (2 microservicios detrás de nginx):\n- nginx :80  -->  /api/  -->  park-app:8080   (parqueo principal)\n- nginx :80  -->  /users/ -->  users-service:8686 (perfiles de usuario)\n\nAutenticación: JWT de AWS Cognito (user pool us-east-1_DHnNHfkCk).\n1) Corre la petición '🔑 Auth > Login (Cognito)' con tu usuario/clave PUCE.\n   El script guarda automáticamente el IdToken en la variable {{idToken}}.\n2) Todas las demás peticiones usan ese token como Bearer (heredado a nivel de colección).\n\nRoles: USER (estudiante), GUARD (guardia), ADMIN. Cada endpoint indica en su descripción qué rol necesita.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{idToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "cognitoUrl",
      "value": "https://cognito-idp.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "clientId",
      "value": "4vhmgbe076v27ub5mu9ru8jo8l",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "username",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "idToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "mes",
      "value": "2026-08",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "🔑 Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (Cognito)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "if (json.AuthenticationResult) {",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('idToken', json.AuthenticationResult.IdToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.AuthenticationResult.AccessToken);",
                  "    console.log('✅ IdToken guardado en {{idToken}}');",
                  "    pm.test('Login OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "} else {",
                  "    console.log('🔴 Login falló:', pm.response.text());",
                  "    pm.test('Login falló', () => { throw new Error('Sin AuthenticationResult'); });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "auth": {
              "type": "noauth"
            },
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/x-amz-json-1.1"
              },
              {
                "key": "X-Amz-Target",
                "value": "AWSCognitoIdentityProviderService.InitiateAuth"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"AuthFlow\": \"USER_PASSWORD_AUTH\",\n  \"ClientId\": \"{{clientId}}\",\n  \"AuthParameters\": {\n    \"USERNAME\": \"{{username}}\",\n    \"PASSWORD\": \"{{password}}\"\n  }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{cognitoUrl}}",
              "host": [
                "{{cognitoUrl}}"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Autentica contra AWS Cognito (USER_PASSWORD_AUTH). Va DIRECTO a Cognito, no por nginx. Rellena {{username}} y {{password}} en las variables de la colección. El script de test guarda el IdToken automáticamente."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
